WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.000
Protoculture.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.030
A highly advanced alien race

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:13.420
that became the first spacefaring civilization in the Milky Way 500,000 years ago.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:18.890
By manipulating the genes of 
primitive indigenous life forms,

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:24.780
they sowed the seeds that would eventually bloom into the various humanoid cultures of the galaxy.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:30.590
Vestiges of their power can still be found throughout the Milky Way.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.350
The enemy has deployed an entire fleet and multiple surveillance satellites.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.100
<i>Silent hacker</i>

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:49.450
Let's own their defense network so we can get through.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.990
This is going to be a fun ride.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.220
Every door

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.530
is meant to be

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.370
opened.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.210
<i>A flashing impression</i>

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.480
<i>as I find your heart's hidden backdoor</i>

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>Words unheard, a rhythm unknown</i>

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.560
<i>In a chilling light</i>

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.640
<i>I send you my feelings as they are</i>

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:29.100
<i>and in this warped time, I hear your voice</i>

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:38.530
<i>The sky burns and the galaxy awaits</i>

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:48.070
<i>With everyone gone, you're still not alone</i>

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.540
<i>I want to know the real you</i>

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.290
<i>Rename sadness to something else</i>

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.340
<i>and use your avatar to hide your wounds</i>

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.310
<i>I'm here to help you</i>

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.930
<i>The hand of sadness might reach you</i>

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.560
Holy moly.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.940
<i>but its touch is just the proof you're alive</i>

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.310
Checkmate.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.060
<i>Don't forget it</i>

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:18.700
<i>that I'm here with you</i>

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.080
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.930
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.790
<i>Let's share a selfish kiss</i>

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.590
<i>The petals of this flower fall in the wind</i>

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:47.060
<i>The stars are more than I could count</i>

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.600
<i>I could place all the blame on you,</i>

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.350
<i>swallowing back my tears,</i>

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:58.240
<i>but I can't tell anyone about how my heart races</i>

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.410
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.700
<i>Until it all breaks apart</i>

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.650
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.880
<i>Until you can take flight</i>

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.370
<i>(To the ends)</i>

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.250
<i>Deep in my heart</i>

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.990
<i>(Of time)</i>

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.790
<i>There is a prayer</i>

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.710
<i>Just feel, just believe</i>

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.810
<i>and speed through it all</i>

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.970
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.720
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.310
<i>Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me</i>

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.940
<i>I'll leave my body behind</i>

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.940
<i>I'll leave my heart beating hard</i>

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:39.370
<i>I'll break free from these chains holding me down</i>

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:46.080
<i>Just come get me, in my purest form</i>

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:56.740
Planet Voldor

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.910
62% of Voldor's landmass is covered in marshes.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.960
A blue and green planet.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:03.690
Its principal exports are lumber, fruits, and spring water.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.760
Zero strategic value.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.480
Makina, Reina, First Lt. Messer and I will infiltrate the capital from the south.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.690
Mikumo and Freyja will enter from the north with Second Lt. Mirage and Sgt. Hayate.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.650
Mew got it!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.920
No cat puns allowed.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.100
Apawlogies.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:25.910
Oh. My. God. Rei-Rei, you're the cutest kitty ever!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:25.910
Hiss.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.160
Don't scratch me.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.310
I'm allergic to cats, you know.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.490
Voldorians were originally 
modified felines.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.920
Get out if you're just going to complain.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.340
Mew can't lose either, Hayate!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.590
I know.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.760
Yeah. I can't lose.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:51.770
<i>We don't need someone who 
lets inane words get to her.</i>

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.070
Just you watch me, Mikumo!

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.670
I'll show you I can be useful!

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.520
Wait, what?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.880
Kumo-Kumo left ages ago.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.070
She's the queen lone wolf.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.450
Not again...

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.690
Impawsible...

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.340
So many kinds of cat ears!

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.300
This is the best!

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.310
There's no sign of any major disturbance.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.010
Their bio-fold waves are off the charts.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.550
Kaname.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.980
On it.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.980
Excuse me!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.900
Could you tell me where the river bus boards—

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.210
Watch your step.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.320
Excuse me? <i>Your</i> big ass ran into me!

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.280
Ah, I'm so sorry!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.330
Analysis complete.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.290
As we thought. Seidznole detected.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.530
That's what's causing the Var.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:09.160
We can assume both the army and police are under mind control.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.410
God dammit...

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.190
Oh, my poor boy! Are you okay?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.810
You have a cold?

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.590
I have the most wonderful catnip!

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:25.030
Don't worry about him!

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.240
My goodness, can't you even hold back a sneeze?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.100
Easier said than done!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.310
Why are we even doing this infiltration crap?

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.300
We're pilots.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.460
My thoughts exactly. However...

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.820
Experiences build character.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:47.190
"The deeper a jellyfish has swum, the more delicious it is."

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:48.170
Apparently.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.880
I'm not a jellyfish.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.640
Neither am I!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:55.500
It's okay! Just leave this to me!

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:59.630
I've been trained on how to operate behind enemy lines between dance classes!

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.400
What's wrong?

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.070
This scent...

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.900
Run-run, yippee!

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.950
The stealthiest of all operations.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.370
Why does everybody have to be like this?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.160
This brings back mewmories!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.480
Are these Windermerean exdel apples?

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.580
You've got quite the nose!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.840
They're from Windermere?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.520
Domestic purroduce got restricted. Though these aren't bad.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.300
Right, miss—

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.160
Delish!

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:43.390
She really ought to be a bit more careful.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.020
Give her a break. We got some intel.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.440
That these apples are from Windermere.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.100
And how is that useful at all?

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.420
I can hear it.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.450
What is it this time?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.450
This color...

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:10.260
<i>Words alone can't convey</i>

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:19.680
<i>the truths I carry in my heart</i>

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:21.660
Such a sad color...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:27.760
<i>One might know them, but not erase</i>

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.640
What are they doing?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.190
I know that insignia.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:35.810
<i>Sadness can be</i>

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:35.950
Captain Alberto Larrazábal, the ace pilot of NUNS's Voldor fleet.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.120
Dad! Answer us, dad!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:44.460
<i>cured by smiles over time</i>

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.330
"Dad"?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:46.380
This is the Walküre song that 
makes people feel better, right?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.790
<i>Don't forget that I love you</i>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.790
Answer us, dad!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:53.360
<i>There's a reason{inaudible}</i>

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.320
I-865. The wind is changing.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.800
Your shift is over.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:57.760
Roger.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.260
Dad!

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:04.890
Daddy!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.840
They have their best pilots doing grunt work?

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.360
This is so wrong.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.320
It's a lie. I knew some stupid song wouldn't heal him.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:17.350
But it's not...

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.030
Walküre's songs can.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:20.510
Hey!

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:21.040
Freyja!

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.170
Freyja!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.050
Cut it out!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.300
Let go of her!

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.700
You're so useless.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:39.010
I know your voice.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.680
You've got time to spare?

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.720
Mikumo?

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.020
Where have you been all this time?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.680
What's that? That's a weird bug.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.910
It's a cicada-shaped micro-drone.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.270
It has both sensors and cameras.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:56.900
Sensors and cameras?

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:59.870
A top secret inter-government meeting?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:00.820
Yes.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.710
We ought to learn something interesting from this.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:10.670
So many... When did you install them?

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.520
Looks like it's beginning.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.580
Lord Roid?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:25.600
Integration into the NUG wasn't all that bad either.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:31.860
Their bases gave us jobs and technology.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.390
Buying locals like that is how they do things.

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:40.360
Still, aren't your demands a bit too much?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.580
Declaring war, no less...

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.040
We don't have much time.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:50.920
The average life span of 
Windermereans, if I recall correctly,

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.610
is about 30 years.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.670
Indeed.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:01.000
Very well. We'll behave.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:07.680
Windermereans like to blow up foes and friends indiscriminately

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.890
using dimensional weapons.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.050
Dimensional weapons?

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.250
I can only hope you haven't already brought those here.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.190
Oh, please.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.460
Then what are you doing at those ruins?

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:22.280
Just academic research.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:28.000
I forgot you were a scientist as well.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.790
I have read your papers on the Protoculture.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:38.000
"The last humanoid races the 
dying Protoculture gave birth to

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.220
were the ones here in the Brisingr Cluster.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:47.390
Therefore we are, by all means, the rightful heirs of the Protoculture."

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.720
Or so I recall.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.350
Do you really believe those words?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:57.580
The key to that mystery may lie in those very ruins.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.000
Ruins?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.860
I found it.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:04.990
The Paraganal ruins. Seems to have once belonged to the Protoculture.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:06.840
Kaname?

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.700
The Voldorians consider it a holy place.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:15.500
The Windermereans locked it down and built some kind of facility there.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.620
There's a dimensional weapon there?

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.110
We can't dismiss the possibility.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:22.930
Roger. Let's meet up.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.740
Intruders. It seems our air 
defense lines have been hacked.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:32.940
I see.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:42.570
What's this dimensional weapon 
thing you were talking about?

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.500
It distorts space-time to cause destruction.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:48.490
It's an extremely powerful weapon of mass destruction.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.120
Banned according to the galactic treaties,

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.300
but they say seven years ago Windermere deployed one

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.560
during their war of independence.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.520
Seven years ago?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.430
Maybe that thing?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.100
But they said Earthlings did that.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:13.130
No. Windermere used it against the NUNS.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:15.350
Millions of civilians fell victim to it.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.810
But our elder said...

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.780
Is the me you see the real me?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.610
Or...

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:34.460
Heinz.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.040
Father?

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:43.020
A dark wind blows through your heart.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.380
Did you see the hole?

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:55.890
That hole was bored into the 
hearts of all Windermereans.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:14:00.280
The only way to fill it is revenge.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.200
As you say, Father.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.280
Good work, Kumo-Kumo.

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.910
You too.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:20.380
Whoa. Those are the Protoculture ruins?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.500
That's a lot of culture!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.240
What is this wind?

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.120
Just you look, Mikumo!

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:32.060
This time for real, I'll show you—

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.970
She left again.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.810
How's security?

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:45.110
All trash. Junk. Not even exciting.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.950
They're armed to the teeth.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.660
Doesn't look like academic research to me.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.830
Let's begin, Makina.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:03.290
Okies! Let's find out what's in the secret plant!

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.090
<i>Hello</i>

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.410
<i>Hello</i>

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:19.790
<i>Hip and hop as the clock ticks and tocks{jikujiku na jukujuku}</i>

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.560
<i>Restlessly flutter around like a butterfly{zowazowa kanari gyowagyowa}</i>

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:28.530
<i>Don't stare at me so impatiently{chirichiri to jirojiro to kocchi minaide}</i>

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:34.390
<i>I'm so tired, glittering with— oh give me a break!{betobeto dashi giragira iranai no yo hiyahiya}</i>

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:41.280
<i>Tingle-tingle? Something's wrong... My heart's out of control{chikun chikun okashii na? hato no seigyo fukanou jtiai}</i>

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:47.720
<i>Thimpety thump, it won't stop. No one told me about this!{tokidoki dokidoki dokudokutte konna watashi wa shiranai}</i>

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:53.530
<i>Feelings rolling all around the clock{kokoro korokoro chikutaku furiko ga tomaranai}</i>

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:56.350
<i>I'm so awkward when I'm around you{aimai i my me and you}</i>

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:59.460
<i>I feel like I'm some bugged robot{kore wa gatagata gosadou}</i>

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:02.230
<i>Please just ignore me, this doesn't count{sou yo kaunto shinaide}</i>

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:10.160
<i>I'm just tingling all over, walking the edge{jirijiri jirijin hirihiri hirirhin shiteru dake}</i>

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.580
Holy moly.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.100
They're in perfect sync.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:12.150
It took them a while to get there.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:18.220
They didn't used to get along. They'd start fighting the moment they saw each other.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:21.040
We've had shows canceled because of them.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.810
<i>Want? Can't! Won't. I'm me and you're mine{aitai aenai awanai me mine}</i>

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:25.630
Water and oil, mixing not recommended.

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:25.630
<i>Don't wanna see you, but maybe I do. I'm me and you're mine{aitaku mo nai aimai me mine}</i>

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.690
<i>Want? Can't! Won't! I still wanna see you!{aitai aenai awanai aitai}</i>

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.730
Here we are!

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.310
Who knew there'd be such a huge cave under the ruins?

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:46.090
All sensors and cameras are sleeping like logs.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:49.480
We've got 30 minutes until the 
next guard patrol gets here.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.110
What's with this place? It's filled with silos.

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:57.530
And they're full of... water?

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.750
Maybe it's used for cooling the dimensional weapon?

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.220
No.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:04.560
Found this in a container over there.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.420
Seems to be plain drinking water.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.380
I've seen it in army facilities before.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.060
What a letdown.

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.090
We came all the way here for water?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.540
But isn't it a bit <i>too</i> much water?

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:18.490
It's water used by the army.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:28.650
61.4% of Var cases so far have been in the military.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.200
Wait a moment!

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.990
Windermere is using the water from here?

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.160
Who are you, beckoning me?

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:55.340
Protoculture?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.610
Results?

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:01.150
Sodium: 1.1%.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.600
Potassium: 0.17%.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:07.470
Voldor bicarbonate: 0.03%.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:08.730
Just regular water.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:09.710
Oh.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:14.320
Look what I've found! Looks yummy!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:19.710
Galactic apples? Must also be for the military.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:23.530
It's cheap but high on nutrients. Highly convenient.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:27.960
Galactic apples... Officially Windermere apples.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.880
It's a little known fact.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:32.370
Really?

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:36.380
So everyone was unknowingly 
eating Windermerean apples?

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.480
What are you doing, Makina?

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.600
Doing some taste testing.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.730
Polyphenols and vitamin C.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.560
It's just an apple.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:52.440
Just what are you up to, Windermere?

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:55.480
They found us?

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:58.940
But you've got all security 
systems on lockdown, Rei-Rei!

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:03.270
The wind has been disrupted.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:06.080
I repeat. The wind has been disrupted.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.830
Find the intruders and capture them.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.000
Filthy Earthlings.

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.840
Makina, Reina, secure our escape route.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.510
Everyone else, gather as many samples as you can.

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:17.460
Roger.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.900
Watch our backs, Messer.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:20.590
Roger.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:25.450
We're taking back regular water and apples?

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:26.790
No questions. Hurry!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:32.380
Galactic apples... Windermere apples...

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.380
Close these shutters.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:37.480
If we lock this and that,

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:38.440
it'll be perfect.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.700
Impossible combination.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:43.740
Dangerous to mix.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.460
The polyphenols bound to the Voldor bicarbonate.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.720
Detecting high concentration of seidznole.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:01.660
Not half bad.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:06.220
So if you mix water from here with Windermere apples,

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:10.100
it creates seidznole in the body that triggers the Var.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:15.060
Other planets' ruins probably have water with similar composition.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:19.930
Windermere artificially spreads the Var using the water and apples.

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:22.950
They then controls the victims with the song of the wind.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.410
They use Windermere apples like that?

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.370
Make a left over there!

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:51.980
<i>You couldn't catch up, so you always</i>

00:20:51.980 --> 00:21:01.150
<i>looked up at something from here</i>

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.160
Mikumo?

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.940
What are you doing?!

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:06.840
Hurry!

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.230
Fre-Fre!

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.540
Go on ahead!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.100
We'll catch up right away!

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:15.950
I'm leaving those two in your hands!

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.060
Let's go.

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:27.550
This way. Hurry.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:37.690
Let's go.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:47.320
Three fell into the trap.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.700
Two NUG dogs...

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:56.160
And one Windermere traitor.

00:21:57.990 --> 00:21:59.970
The Aerial Knights!

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:02.900
The enemy...

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.840
Mission 07: Behind Enemy Lines

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.680
Are you ready?

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:26.860
<i>I heard a rumor that the world's gonna end someday</i>

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:32.370
<i>Just kidding, it's obviously a lie</i>

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:37.710
<i>I remember looking up at the sky</i>

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:41.420
<i>and feeling like I was in the future</i>

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:47.020
<i>I felt completely in sync with your wind</i>

00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:56.020
<i>You make me truly feel like a girl</i>

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:03.520
<i>so I've got no choice but to do it. I can't stop now!</i>

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.110
You better be ready!

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:08.700
<i>If my rune shines with a flash</i>

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:12.450
<i>wow woh wow woh</i>

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:15.940
<i>I fall in love</i>

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:19.410
<i>wow woh wow woh</i>

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:24.960
<i>Lalali lalala you make me</i>

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:32.750
<i>Lalala rune pika invincible</i>

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.900
Next time: Escape Resonance
